{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013SUQRhuuFRZCQp4LGcVVdh","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: rel01.0-uc001-wc\n     2→title: \"Count lines, words, and bytes via wc\"\n     3→\n     4→summary: |\n     5→  The operator runs the Go wc binary on one or more files or stdin. The binary counts\n     6→  lines, words, and bytes (or characters, or max line length) and writes formatted results\n     7→  to stdout. The differential testing harness then runs both the Go binary and the Homebrew\n     8→  reference binary (gwc from coreutils) with the same stdin, args, and environment and\n     9→  confirms that their outputs are identical byte-for-byte. No output normalization is\n    10→  needed because wc output consists of deterministic integer counts.\n    11→\n    12→actor: Human Operator\n    13→\n    14→trigger: |\n    15→  The operator has completed the PRD (prd005-wc.yaml) and invokes do-work to produce\n    16→  a passing differential test for cmd/wc.\n    17→\n    18→flow:\n    19→  - id: F1\n    20→    step: |\n    21→      The operator runs the Go wc binary with stdin input or file arguments.\n    22→      Example: printf 'foo\\nbar baz\\n' | ./bin/wc\n    23→  - id: F2\n    24→    step: |\n    25→      cmd/wc reads from stdin or the named files. For each input, it counts newlines (-l),\n    26→      words (-w), bytes (-c), characters (-m), and max line length (-L) as requested by the\n    27→      active flags. When no flags are given, it counts lines, words, and bytes.\n    28→  - id: F3\n    29→    step: |\n    30→      cmd/wc writes one line per input in the format \"COUNT COUNT COUNT FILENAME\" with\n    31→      right-aligned columns. For stdin with no filename, the filename is omitted.\n    32→  - id: F4\n    33→    step: |\n    34→      When multiple files are given, cmd/wc prints a \"total\" line with the sum of all counts.\n    35→  - id: F5\n    36→    step: |\n    37→      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/wc and gwc with\n    38→      the same stdin, args, and environment.\n    39→  - id: F6\n    40→    step: |\n    41→      The harness compares stdout byte-for-byte with no normalization. Both binaries must\n    42→      produce identical count values and column alignment.\n    43→  - id: F7\n    44→    step: |\n    45→      If the outputs match, the test passes. If they diverge, the harness reports the\n    46→      triggering args, both outputs, and both exit codes.\n    47→\n    48→touchpoints:\n    49→  - T1: \"cmd/wc — line, word, byte, char, max-line-length counting, multi-file totals (prd005-wc R1, R2, R3, R4, R5, R6)\"\n    50→  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, binary execution and comparison\"\n    51→\n    52→success_criteria:\n    53→  - id: S1\n    54→    criterion: cmd/wc compiles and ./bin/wc exists after mage build.\n    55→  - id: S2\n    56→    criterion: |\n    57→      printf 'foo\\nbar baz\\n' | ./bin/wc produces '2 3 12' (matching gwc output format).\n    58→  - id: S3\n    59→    criterion: |\n    60→      The differential test for default mode passes: ./bin/wc and gwc produce identical\n    61→      output on three-line stdin.\n    62→  - id: S4\n    63→    criterion: |\n    64→      The differential tests for -l, -w, and -c flags each pass: outputs match gwc\n    65→      byte-for-byte.\n    66→  - id: S5\n    67→    criterion: |\n    68→      The differential test for -m with LC_ALL=C passes: character count matches byte\n    69→      count under the C locale.\n    70→  - id: S6\n    71→    criterion: |\n    72→      The differential test for -L passes: max line length matches gwc on multi-line input\n    73→      with varying line lengths.\n    74→  - id: S7\n    75→    criterion: |\n    76→      The differential test for multi-file with total line passes: right-aligned columns\n    77→      and the \"total\" label match gwc output byte-for-byte.\n    78→  - id: S8\n    79→    criterion: |\n    80→      Empty stdin produces '0 0 0' for default flags, matching gwc.\n    81→  - id: S9\n    82→    criterion: |\n    83→      A non-existent file argument produces an error to stderr, exits 1, and still processes\n    84→      other files on the command line, matching gwc behavior.\n    85→\n    86→out_of_scope:\n    87→  - --files0-from is covered in the test suite but is not the primary flow of this use case.\n    88→  - --total=always and --total=only are covered in the test suite but are not part of the primary flow.\n    89→  - Binary input edge cases are covered in the test suite but are not the primary flow.\n    90→\n    91→test_suite: test-rel01.0\n    92→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99be3374-9d46-4b9e-9096-dd7e107a70c8","uuid":"085c84cf-57f1-4b34-9684-fe6150ea7f20","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/115/docs/specs/use-cases/rel01.0-uc001-wc.yaml","content":"id: rel01.0-uc001-wc\ntitle: \"Count lines, words, and bytes via wc\"\n\nsummary: |\n  The operator runs the Go wc binary on one or more files or stdin. The binary counts\n  lines, words, and bytes (or characters, or max line length) and writes formatted results\n  to stdout. The differential testing harness then runs both the Go binary and the Homebrew\n  reference binary (gwc from coreutils) with the same stdin, args, and environment and\n  confirms that their outputs are identical byte-for-byte. No output normalization is\n  needed because wc output consists of deterministic integer counts.\n\nactor: Human Operator\n\ntrigger: |\n  The operator has completed the PRD (prd005-wc.yaml) and invokes do-work to produce\n  a passing differential test for cmd/wc.\n\nflow:\n  - id: F1\n    step: |\n      The operator runs the Go wc binary with stdin input or file arguments.\n      Example: printf 'foo\\nbar baz\\n' | ./bin/wc\n  - id: F2\n    step: |\n      cmd/wc reads from stdin or the named files. For each input, it counts newlines (-l),\n      words (-w), bytes (-c), characters (-m), and max line length (-L) as requested by the\n      active flags. When no flags are given, it counts lines, words, and bytes.\n  - id: F3\n    step: |\n      cmd/wc writes one line per input in the format \"COUNT COUNT COUNT FILENAME\" with\n      right-aligned columns. For stdin with no filename, the filename is omitted.\n  - id: F4\n    step: |\n      When multiple files are given, cmd/wc prints a \"total\" line with the sum of all counts.\n  - id: F5\n    step: |\n      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/wc and gwc with\n      the same stdin, args, and environment.\n  - id: F6\n    step: |\n      The harness compares stdout byte-for-byte with no normalization. Both binaries must\n      produce identical count values and column alignment.\n  - id: F7\n    step: |\n      If the outputs match, the test passes. If they diverge, the harness reports the\n      triggering args, both outputs, and both exit codes.\n\ntouchpoints:\n  - T1: \"cmd/wc — line, word, byte, char, max-line-length counting, multi-file totals (prd005-wc R1, R2, R3, R4, R5, R6)\"\n  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, binary execution and comparison\"\n\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - id: S1\n    criterion: cmd/wc compiles and ./bin/wc exists after mage build.\n  - id: S2\n    criterion: |\n      printf 'foo\\nbar baz\\n' | ./bin/wc produces '2 3 12' (matching gwc output format).\n  - id: S3\n    criterion: |\n      The differential test for default mode passes: ./bin/wc and gwc produce identical\n      output on three-line stdin.\n  - id: S4\n    criterion: |\n      The differential tests for -l, -w, and -c flags each pass: outputs match gwc\n      byte-for-byte.\n  - id: S5\n    criterion: |\n      The differential test for -m with LC_ALL=C passes: character count matches byte\n      count under the C locale.\n  - id: S6\n    criterion: |\n      The differential test for -L passes: max line length matches gwc on multi-line input\n      with varying line lengths.\n  - id: S7\n    criterion: |\n      The differential test for multi-file with total line passes: right-aligned columns\n      and the \"total\" label match gwc output byte-for-byte.\n  - id: S8\n    criterion: |\n      Empty stdin produces '0 0 0' for default flags, matching gwc.\n  - id: S9\n    criterion: |\n      A non-existent file argument produces an error to stderr, exits 1, and still processes\n      other files on the command line, matching gwc behavior.\n\nout_of_scope:\n  - --files0-from is covered in the test suite but is not the primary flow of this use case.\n  - --total=always and --total=only are covered in the test suite but are not part of the primary flow.\n  - Binary input edge cases are covered in the test suite but are not the primary flow.\n\ntest_suite: test-rel01.0\n","numLines":92,"startLine":1,"totalLines":92}}}
